config SECURITY_PROVFS
	bool "provfs: stamp user.prov.* xattrs on writes"
	depends on SECURITY
	default n
	help
	  provfs is a small, stackable Linux Security Module that stamps
	  user.prov.session and user.prov.ts xattrs on every file
	  successfully closed after being opened for write.

	  The session value is "comm:<comm>:pid:<tgid>:uid:<uid>".
	  Files under /proc, /sys, /dev, /run, /tmp, .git, node_modules,
	  target, and the cargo registry are skipped.

	  Pairs with the userspace FUSE-overlay provfs daemon (which
	  handles filesystems that don't support user xattrs natively)
	  and a userspace `prov` CLI for reading the xattrs.

	  See Documentation/admin-guide/LSM/provfs.rst.

	  If unsure, say N.
